						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1399.msg14107#msg14107"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1399.msg14107#msg14107">Re: And so it begins...</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #3 on:</b> February 01, 2005, 03:29:45 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							RN is not nearly as healthy as it appears, 150 in the bazzar in overnight numbers is a sure sign of attrition. Logged in one of the alt acounts a couple times before it canceled last week, and at a couple random times, the bazaar was lucky to come close to 200 traders.<br /><br />Some servers are doing better, made an alt for a sec on 7th hammer, they still have 250-350 over night. A couple others are similar to 7th hammer, but far more are in much worse shape.<br /><br />I can see some of the lower population blues being merged if populations do not improve after DoN releases.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
