							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1399.msg14124#msg14124"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1399.msg14124#msg14124">Re: And so it begins...</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #9 on:</b> February 01, 2005, 06:17:35 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							/shrug i think the population of rodcet is almost perfect.&nbsp; DoN should be a nice expansion, the storylines in lavastorm, dreadlands and overthere might be kinda interesting. SP/MM revamps are nice cause no one went there, pathing can be a little fucked up but nothing you cant work around and raid mobs there in MM have some nice drops for the effort, havent heard of anything in splitpaw yet.<br /><br />i have played, CoH, EQ2, and WoW and all didnt hold my interest. fun for a bit but that was it.<br /><br />prolly the only reason i still play EQ is cause i play for myself and not a guild, playing at my own pace makes the game so much better.
						</td>
					</tr>
