								My Avatar can beat up your avatar!<br />
								<br />
								
								<a href="http://members.msn.com/kinladar@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="kinladar@hotmail.com" border="0" /></a>
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org" title="http://www.rodcetnife.org" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:truman@thewavz.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1399.msg14141#msg14141"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1399.msg14141#msg14141">Re: And so it begins...</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #12 on:</b> February 02, 2005, 08:10:28 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							It&#039;s been slowly dying since PoP. That was when alot of the small family guilds started to fold, and you saw fewer and fewer of them around.<br /><br />They were the real training farms for up and coming players. The progression was alot like:<br /><br />Family Guild --&gt; Midlevel Guild --&gt; High End Guild --&gt; Family Guild <br /><br />But with the loss of the family guilds in general, and some of them trying to restructure as a more raid oriented model, and often dying in the attempt due to the typical drama that comes with a raiding model, or the members not wanting to raid and leaving, it&#039;s been slowly coming apart at the seams.<br /><br />Most of my old friends, in fact I would pretty well safely say all my old friends who were never interested in the raiding aspect have all quit ages ago. <br /><br />And I would safely say that a reduction in the Bazaar Trader numbers is a very clear sign of the health of the server. With more and more gear sellable now with attunable items fairly common, and not that hard to get, the bazaar should be booming.<br /><br />It should have been like when Rune spells were sold by the higher end guilds, and the midlevel, and family guilds bought them up like candy.<br /><br />But there&#039;s not the same market now as there was before.<br /><br />It&#039;s a multiple cause reason why EQ is in the current state that it&#039;s in, and it all comes back to SoE&#039;s plans, and lack of good implementation.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
