						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1399.msg14143#msg14143"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1399.msg14143#msg14143">Re: And so it begins...</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #14 on:</b> February 02, 2005, 08:34:05 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I never suggested DoN will be really outstanding.&nbsp; It won&#039;t.&nbsp; Just that that&#039;s what it would take to somewhat turn things around.&nbsp; Either that or the server farms for EQ2 and WoW need to explode.&nbsp; &nbsp;<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/cwm12.gif" alt="cwm12" border="0" /><br /><br />Not sure what you can say by talking about people buying runes.&nbsp; Muramite runes stayed very expensive for a long time.&nbsp; They&#039;ve finally come down to the 15k range, which for many people still seems high.&nbsp; Of course the price came down as almost everything had throughout EQ.<br /><br />
